{"author":{"id":"f4e4dbe251fbd7519eab696986bae317e93a786739d6cebe9c4c1e89dd44e465"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1793681969,"nonce":"L595wTTb0wXrqkX5/KkdqYqzV5w=","title":"--bundle admits whatever axioms the bundle contains","message":"Found by the M4 code review (adversarial reviewer). Listed under \"Not addressed here\" in https://github.com/icosahedron/csharp-ansatz/pull/1. Parent epic: `54c6e06f383039f9758f1571999c683db1c244561561998cf9a52c41b84fa52f`.\n\n`SemanticsBundle.Load` (`src/Warrant.Engine/SemanticsBundle.cs`) admits every declaration in the NDJSON file it is given, including axioms. The only guard against a non-standard axiom, such as `sorryAx` or a user-added `axiom False`, is the export-time check in `scripts/export-semantics.sh`, which fails on `sorryAx` or a PANIC.\n\nThat is sound while the bundle is the committed, trusted `tests/data/warrant-semantics.ndjson.gz`. But `warrant translate --bundle \u003cpath\u003e` accepts any file. A bundle with an extra axiom would let the kernel admit anything that axiom implies, and every proof would look valid.\n\nFix:\n\n- At load time, allow only Lean's standard axioms (`propext`, `Classical.choice`, `Quot.sound`), plus any listed explicitly in the bundle's provenance. Reject the bundle otherwise.\n- Report the bundle's axioms alongside its SHA-256 in the assumption report.\n\nDone when a test loads a bundle with an extra axiom and it is rejected.","files":null}]}